# One line ending everywhere. Several test files read their own sources as
# text (`include_str!` in src-tauri, the workflow and hook pins in
# apps/desktop) and look for "\n" patterns; a Windows checkout under
# core.autocrlf handed them "\r\n" and five of the shell's tests failed
# before anything was changed. Git still detects binaries by content.
* text=auto eol=lf
# cmd.exe misreads labels in a batch file with bare LF line endings.
*.bat text eol=crlf
# The updater gate fixtures are byte exact: their sha256 and signature files
# pin the bytes as committed, so no line ending rule may touch them.
apps/desktop/ci/fixtures/** -text
# Docs sources sidecars are lists of "claim -> path" lines whose order and
# duplicates carry no meaning: a merge keeps both sides' lines instead of
# stopping on two pull requests that each appended a claim (git's built-in
# union driver, for local merges and rebases of main into a branch).
docs/.sources/**/*.txt merge=union
